  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OPIC in Kosovo 2016-2022 - OPIC in Kosovo 2016-2020</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">OPIC in Kosovo 2016-2022</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">OPIC has presented to Sida a proposal for support to civil society organizations in Kosovo for the period 2016-2020, indicating greater focus on labor rights, gender equality, the empowerment of underrepresented groups and anti-corruption. This concept makes the added value of OPIC clearer, and it is evidently in line with their core activities in Sweden. The programmatic content of the project document coherent with the current program for Kosovo 2012-2015. The required total budget is 25 000 000 SEK.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Olof Palme International Center har presenterat ett f&#xf6;rslag till Sida f&#xf6;r insats till st&#xf6;d till civilsamh&#xe4;llesorganisationer i Kosovo under perioden 2016-2020. J&#xe4;mf&#xf6;rt med tidigare st&#xf6;d inneb&#xe4;r f&#xf6;rslaget ett st&#xf6;rre fokus p&#xe5; arbetstagares och underrepresenterade gruppers r&#xe4;ttigheter, j&#xe4;mst&#xe4;lldhet, samt antikorruption. F&#xf6;rslaget korresponderar d&#xe4;rmed v&#xe4;l med Olof Palme International Centers k&#xe4;rnaktiviteter i Sverige som &#xf6;kar merv&#xe4;rdet av insatsen. Projektet &#xe4;r i &#xf6;vrigt i enlighet med Olof Palme International Centers tidigare projekt f&#xf6;r 2012-2015. Budgeten f&#xf6;r projektet &#xe4;r 25 000 000 SEK.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The OPIC programme objective is &quot;To see citizens, in particular women and youth, and other civil society groups be actively involved in local organisations/or networks and take an active role in governance by influencing the policies, political agendas and decisions in their favour&quot;. The OPC strategy for the Kosovo programme is focused on the following main areas of work: a) citizen participation in decision-making, b) transparency and accountability, c) socio-economic and labour&#xa0; rights, d) support to progressive political parties and movements.
OPIC theory of change &quot; The social transformation and development is achieved through collective organising&quot; is valid and applicable.
All reporting requirements as per the ageement conditions are met. Annual audit report is clean and no deviation from the annual work plan is reported.</narrative>
  </description>
